WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:01.089
Good morning John.

00:00:01.089 --> 00:00:02.089
I'm going to tell you a story.

00:00:02.089 --> 00:00:05.410
So when I first moved to Missoula I went to
the grocery store 'cause I was hungry and

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:08.920
I knew how to make tacos so I bought some
meat and some beef and...

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:09.920
Meat and beef?

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:12.120
Some beans and cheese and tortillas and stuff,
right?

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:14.840
And the cashier, as she's checking me out
is like "Boop.

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:17.280
Boop" and then she's like "So, tacos tonight?"

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:21.530
At this point I was around 23 years old and
I can say pretty securely that I had had,

00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:26.780
like, zero interactions with cashiers that
weren't "Hello", "Thank you" and "Do you want

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:27.780
a receipt?"

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:31.060
So basically, I was completely freaked out,
flabbergasted, I didn't know what to say,

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:35.260
despite the fact that, yes, I was having tacos,
so the clear answer was yes, which I think

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:36.320
I finally came up with.

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:40.920
Having seen that I was not the kind of person
who speaks to people, she didn't push it any

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:43.670
further, so it turns out that I'd moved from
a place where that's not a normal thing to

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:47.270
a place where it was, and also, that I kinda
like it.

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:49.920
I mean, it used to be that I was terrified
to, like, tell the person at Wendy's what

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:53.559
kind of hamburger I wanted, but man, in this
town, you gotta be ready, and some people

00:00:53.559 --> 00:00:55.650
really don't like it, but I, I quite do.

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:58.969
I was at Pita Pit recently, and the person
was like, "So, how's your day been?" and I

00:00:58.969 --> 00:01:01.350
was like, "Really weird, actually!"

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:04.449
And they were like, "Well, that sounds interesting,"
and like, settling in for me to tell them

00:01:04.449 --> 00:01:08.609
about it, but I was like, "But I don't have
time to tell you, I need a pita."

00:01:08.609 --> 00:01:11.590
And then there was a time when I was at a
liquor store, oh my God, the woman looks at

00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:15.899
my ID and she was like, "Oh my God, I would
never have thought that you were so old" and

00:01:15.899 --> 00:01:20.220
that's a nice thing to say, I guess, and then
she was like, "The other day, we had an Asian

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:25.490
in here, and he looked so young, I did not
believe his ID, and he was here with his white

00:01:25.490 --> 00:01:29.399
girlfriend" and I was just like, "I could
never imagine that, I would feel so improper".

00:01:29.399 --> 00:01:33.919
Mind you, while there's a line, I'm not the
only person in the liquor store, and I'm like,

00:01:33.919 --> 00:01:35.959
"Okay, miss, you clearly have issues.

00:01:35.959 --> 00:01:40.509
I don't think I'm the person to deal with
them, so I would like to acquire my brown

00:01:40.509 --> 00:01:44.249
liquor of some sort that you're selling to
me and take it home so that I can drink it

00:01:44.249 --> 00:01:47.149
faster than I normally would have now that
I've had this interaction."

00:01:47.149 --> 00:01:51.479
But mostly, I find that talking to strangers,
whether that's on the street or when we're

00:01:51.479 --> 00:01:55.811
having some kind of commercial interaction
is very pleasant, and I like strangers, I

00:01:55.811 --> 00:01:59.029
like talking to strangers when I'm at a shower,
at a bar, or at a club.

00:01:59.029 --> 00:02:00.340
Is a bar and a club the same thing?

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:06.229
Well, anyway, when I see people on the internet
or on the news, they tend to be less nice

00:02:06.229 --> 00:02:09.459
than the ones that I meet in real life, and
so what I'm saying is, if you wanna get an

00:02:09.459 --> 00:02:15.349
accurate picture of the kind of quality people
exist, you gotta talk to strangers!

00:02:15.349 --> 00:02:16.459
Which is not normal advice.

00:02:16.459 --> 00:02:18.799
Don't get in their cars or anything.

00:02:18.799 --> 00:02:20.560
It's also good practice.

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:24.430
I never was comfortable with it until I just
started doing it all the time.

00:02:24.430 --> 00:02:25.760
The other day at Taco Bell, the woman was
like, "Good morning."

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:29.050
It was like, four o'clock in the afternoon,
and I was like, "Not quite."

00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:32.110
And then I felt a little bad about it 'cause
she looked kind of embarrassed, so I was like,

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:36.090
"Well, don't worry about it, when I'm leaving,
you will say "enjoy your meal", and I will

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:39.409
say "you, too" and then I will feel the way
that you feel now."

00:02:39.409 --> 00:02:42.590
And then, when she gave me my food, she didn't
say "Enjoy your meal", so I couldn't do the

00:02:42.590 --> 00:02:45.840
thing, which I thought was gonna be super
funny.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:49.230
There is a lot going on right now.

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:52.480
NerdCon: Stories is next week, so I'm very
busily prepping for that.

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:55.700
I have to make sure that I'm ready to do all
the things I gotta do, and of course, I've

00:02:55.700 --> 00:03:00.719
been totally overwhelmed by the success of
the Wizard School Kickstarter, oh, so cool!

00:03:00.719 --> 00:03:04.162
We're over 1000% funded, so we're gonna get
to make the game, but that doesn't mean that

00:03:04.162 --> 00:03:07.200
you can't go pledge to the Kickstarter, please
do that, 'cause there are stretch goals, and

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.200
we want to hit them.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:13.120
I'm going to be in Portland and Seattle with
Welcome to Night Vale if you're around those

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:18.189
areas, it is super fun, and I've done it before,
such a good show that these people do.

00:03:18.189 --> 00:03:22.640
And I would also like to announce, for the
first time on this channel, our newest video

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:23.870
project things.

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:30.299
One, Engage by Uplift, a series about dealing
with abuse and sex and the weird nature of

00:03:30.299 --> 00:03:31.989
those things in virtual spaces.

00:03:31.989 --> 00:03:35.659
They're taking on difficult and important
topics direct to camera and in discussion

00:03:35.659 --> 00:03:36.659
formats.

00:03:36.659 --> 00:03:41.189
And also, The Financial Diet, which is a show
about how to live in the world as a young

00:03:41.189 --> 00:03:45.450
person while following your dreams but not
ruining your future.

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:49.019
So if you're interested in any of those things,
they're all around me, you can click on them,

00:03:49.019 --> 00:03:51.719
check them out, John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

